      <section data-section="limits">
        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>One owning application process per history on durable local storage. Serverless or distributed deployments need a separate storage design.</li>
          <li>Local ranking uses light English inflections and can miss paraphrases. Correction priority is a lexical heuristic that can miss implicit changes or link an unrelated revision.</li>
          <li>Answer quality and automatic conflict resolution are unverified.</li>
          <li>Context is historical text. The host keeps execution checkpoints, pending tool work, and side-effect replay rules; memory cannot restart an interrupted executor.</li>
          <li>Total cost includes indexing, updates, navigation, and answering. Shorter final context alone does not prove savings.</li>
          <li>The host owns authentication, authorization, user-to-history mapping, and scheduling.</li>
          <li>The TypeScript runtime has no model-call memoization backend.</li>
        </ul>
